Error Detection and Correction: Block Coding & CRC
Objective
To simulate and analyze the mechanisms of Block Coding (error correction) and Cyclic Redundancy Check (CRC) (error detection) within a Cisco Packet Tracer environment.

Theory
Reliable data transfer depends on identifying and correcting bit-level corruption caused by channel noise.

Block Coding (n, k): Adds *r* redundant bits to *k* data bits to form an *n*-bit codeword. In this lab, it is used to demonstrate single-bit error correction.

CRC: Employs polynomial division (e.g., using a generator polynomial 
